title: 'HRMP: New Deposit Flow'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The relay chain HRMP pallet now sets channel deposits through the new `ChannelDeposits` and
    `OnDepositSet` traits from `hrmp-primitives`, set as `hrmp::Config::DepositProvider`. Each call
    asks the provider with a `DepositAction` saying which sides to set. The provider prices and
    tracks the deposits and reports back through `on_deposit_set`, where the call finishes, so a
    provider on another chain can finish it later. Init and accept on system channels skip it.
    Dropping an open request on offboarding now also frees the sender's request slot.

    `LocalDepositProvider` reserves and unreserves through `Config::Currency` and finishes in the
    same call, so existing runtimes behave as before. Every runtime must now set
    `type DepositProvider`; `LocalDepositProvider<Runtime>` works as a drop-in.

    Its covering and preparing for integration of taking deposits on the hrmp-para pallet (CT or AH).
    Right now its just integrating ChannelDeposits into hrmp.
crates:
- name: hrmp-primitives
  bump: minor
- name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
  bump: major
- name: westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: rococo-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-hrmp-relay
  bump: none
- name: polkadot-sdk-frame
  bump: none
